From: reelee81 <reelee81@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:36:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] fitz: Saturate the tile range of a pattern.

fz_draw_end_tile() converted the first and last tile numbers to int with
a plain cast. For an empty area they can be far outside the int range
(about 6e9 in a test file): x86 gives INT_MIN, ARM saturates at the int
limits. The conversion now saturates on every platform, as ARM did, so
the range is the same everywhere. It needs 0015.

Modified for ReePDF on 2026-11-12.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 source/fitz/draw-device.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/fitz/draw-device.c b/source/fitz/draw-device.c
index 72c45fd..5834612 100644
--- a/source/fitz/draw-device.c
+++ b/source/fitz/draw-device.c
@@ -2997,10 +2997,10 @@ fz_draw_end_tile(fz_context *ctx, fz_device *devp)
 	extra_y = tile_tmp.y1 - tile_tmp.y0 - ystep;
 	if (extra_y < 0)
 		extra_y = 0;
-	x0 = floorf((area.x0-1 - tile_tmp.x0 - extra_x) / xstep);
-	y0 = floorf((area.y0-1 - tile_tmp.y0 - extra_y) / ystep);
-	x1 = ceilf((area.x1+1 - tile_tmp.x0 + extra_x) / xstep);
-	y1 = ceilf((area.y1+1 - tile_tmp.y0 + extra_y) / ystep);
+	x0 = fz_saturate_float_to_int(floorf((area.x0-1 - tile_tmp.x0 - extra_x) / xstep));
+	y0 = fz_saturate_float_to_int(floorf((area.y0-1 - tile_tmp.y0 - extra_y) / ystep));
+	x1 = fz_saturate_float_to_int(ceilf((area.x1+1 - tile_tmp.x0 + extra_x) / xstep));
+	y1 = fz_saturate_float_to_int(ceilf((area.y1+1 - tile_tmp.y0 + extra_y) / ystep));
 
 	ctm.e = state[1].dest->x;
 	ctm.f = state[1].dest->y;
